repository-code: "https://github.com/DavidVFeldman/compactness-clique-size"
abstract: >-
  A topological space has finite, respectively bounded, cliques iff every closed
  irreflexive binary relation on it has cliques of finite, respectively bounded
  finite, size. Every compact space has bounded cliques; having finite cliques
  implies limit-point compactness and is implied by omega-limit point compactness,
  so that for T1 spaces it is equivalent to countable compactness. Whether some
  countably compact space has finite but unbounded cliques is the main question
  raised in the note. This repository contains the note together with its Lean 4
  formalization, machine-checked against Mathlib v4.28.0 with no sorries and no
  axioms beyond propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.
keywords:
  - topology
  - compactness
  - countable compactness
  - orthogonality relation
  - clique number
  - chromatic number
  - star-covering properties
